      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "La vez pasada, Hefesto se casó con Afrodita, la diosa del amor. Pero ella amaba a Ares, el dios de la guerra.",
          "en": "Last time, Hephaestus married Aphrodite, the goddess of love. But she loved Ares, the god of war."
        },
        {
          "es": "Esta historia es muy antigua. Homero la cuenta en la Odisea, su gran poema sobre un largo viaje a casa.",
          "en": "This story is very old. Homer tells it in the Odyssey, his great poem about a long journey home."
        },
        {
          "es": "En el poema, un cantor ciego llamado Demódoco la canta en un banquete real.",
          "en": "In the poem, a blind singer named Demodocus sings it at a royal feast."
        },
        {
          "es": "Canta que Ares iba en secreto a la casa de Hefesto cada vez que el herrero no estaba.",
          "en": "He sings that Ares came to the house of Hephaestus in secret, whenever the smith was away."
        },
        {
          "es": "Le llevaba a Afrodita muchos regalos. Y los dos creían que nadie los veía.",
          "en": "He brought Aphrodite many gifts. And they both believed that no one could see them."
        }
      ],
