      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Apenas quedaron libres, los dos amantes huyeron en direcciones opuestas.",
          "en": "The moment they were free, the two lovers fled in opposite directions."
        },
        {
          "es": "Ares corrió al norte, a Tracia, una tierra salvaje y tormentosa de guerreros.",
          "en": "Ares rushed north to Thrace, a wild and stormy land of warriors."
        },
        {
          "es": "Afrodita voló sobre el mar hasta Chipre, la isla donde había nacido de la espuma.",
          "en": "Aphrodite flew over the sea to Cyprus, the island where she was born from the foam."
        },
        {
          "es": "Allí, en su templo de Pafos, las Gracias, diosas de la alegría, la bañaron y la vistieron con ropas hermosas.",
          "en": "There, at her temple in Paphos, the Graces, goddesses of joy, bathed her and dressed her in lovely clothes."
        },
        {
          "es": "Y Hefesto volvió a su fragua, solo.",
          "en": "And Hephaestus went back to his forge, alone."
        }
      ],
